    "Part 5 (Conclusion): Synthesise — markets are a powerful but imperfect allocator; a mixed economy uses government intervention to correct clear cases of market failure while preserving the efficiency gains from markets. The thesis holds: intervention is justified where the benefits of correcting a failure outweigh the costs of intervening.",
